# Only pom.xml and src/ are actually needed to build the image (Dockerfile's multi-stage `mvn
# package`). Everything else here is host-side tooling/docs/config that has zero effect on the
# built jar but, without this file, still busts COPY's cache layer on every edit - see
# router_cpp/.dockerignore's matching note. config/ is deliberately excluded: it's bind-mounted at
# compose runtime (see docker-compose.yml), not baked into this image (Dockerfile.prod, which has
# no runtime bind mount, COPYs it explicitly instead).
build_router.md
resilience.md
stress_run.sh
run_test.sh
run_tests.sh
start.sh
stop.sh
dockerstart.sh
monitor.sh
monitor_stop.sh
monitor/
test_resilience.py
test_resilience.sh
test_csv_files/
config/
target/
logs/
